{
  "about": "Invented cases for the Overview of a month (issue 'Reports and Overview', ADR 0007). Both the server and the app run this file. Each case sets up a person's data (`settings`, a saved `salary_month` with its `fixed_items`, `transactions`, and `debts` with their `repayments`) and asks for the Overview of `month` in `currency` (`null`: leave the parameter out, so the Settings default applies). `expected` is the answer without `month` and `currency`. All amounts are decimal strings of the currency's digits. balance = salary + recurring_income + income_transactions - fixed_costs - purchases + debt_repayments_received - debt_repayments_made. A month paid twice follows the pay cycle of the Settings pay days (20 and 5 unless set): its first part runs from the 20th to the 4th of the next month, its second from the 5th to the 19th, and the month is both together. An income joins the part whose pay day is nearest to its date unless the case names a part. The salary figures are those of salary/tests/vectors.json.",
